      "type": "narrative",
      "id": "anchor",
      "markdown": "## Ship or hold the dual-lineage boundary\n\n- **What:** a change that keeps Claude and Codex apart while they explore, so each opinion stays independent until one settle step (TSK-042).\n- **Why it matters:** if the lanes share context early, the second opinion stops being a second opinion.\n- **Where it stands:** built and reviewed; every check is green except the native Windows canary, which has not run.\n- **You decide:** ship now with the canary as a follow-up, or hold until it runs."
    },
